{{!
    @template tool_vae/attest_declaration

    The declaration as the screens of attestation, withdrawal, pieces and precision draw it: the warning of its anchor
    first, when there is one, then the declaration, with nothing between them.

    The template holds no logic. Two keys are HTML (triple braces): warninghtml, drawn by the template
    tool_vae/anchor_warning (empty when the anchor holds); declarationhtml, drawn by the template tool_vae/declaration.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * warninghtml - HTML, the warning, or an empty string
    * declarationhtml - HTML, the declaration

    Example context (json):
    {
        "warninghtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-warning\" role=\"alert\">The record was renamed.</div>",
        "declarationhtml": "<dl class=\"tool-vae-claim\"><dt>R</dt><dd>RS5</dd></dl><div class=\"tool-vae-situation\">A</div>"
    }
}}
{{{warninghtml}}}{{{declarationhtml}}}
